+\subsection{Data Processing and Evidence Flow}
+Figure~\ref{fig:dataprocessing} is the reviewer-facing processing trace. EchoForge first samples scenario groups from public-proxy strata, then expands each group into phase records, generates synthetic IQ and cue products, materializes detector-view features through a denylisted schema, locks EI discovery and calibration on train/CV rows, and scores the blind holdout once. The important split boundary is early: group IDs, split keys, labels, and audit headers can be inspected by validation code but are denied to model-facing features. This is why the main tables separate selected-threshold TP/FP/FN counts from swept Recall@$\\leq$1\\%FPR and from LCB95.
+
+\begin{figure*}[t]
+  \centering
+  \includegraphics[width=0.98\textwidth]{data_processing_flow.pdf}
+  \caption{End-to-end data-processing path. Scenario groups and phase records generate synthetic radar/cue products; detector-view materialization enforces feature denylisting; train/CV rows drive candidate discovery and calibration; the blind holdout is scored once after selection lock. The figure is a traceability diagram, not an additional performance claim.}
+  \label{fig:dataprocessing}
+\end{figure*}
+
+\begin{table*}[t]
+  \caption{Data Processing Traceability Checklist}
+  \label{tab:dataprocessing}
+  \centering
+  \small
+  \begin{tabular}{@{}p{0.18\textwidth}p{0.24\textwidth}p{0.26\textwidth}p{0.22\textwidth}@{}}
+    \toprule
+    Stage & Produced artifact & Reviewer check & Failure mode guarded \\
+    \midrule
+    Scenario sampling & \texttt{scenario\_manifest.csv}, \texttt{dataset\_manifest.json} & group IDs and split roles exist before phase expansion & row-level leakage through repeated phases \\
+    Sensing synthesis & \texttt{records.csv}, raw IQ shards, cue summaries & phase rows inherit group split and public-proxy priors & undocumented signal-source mixing \\
+    Detector views & detector-view CSVs and schema evidence & labels, group IDs, split keys, and generator metadata are blocked & shortcut learning from audit headers \\
+    EI discovery & \texttt{selection\_lock.json}, component weights, aliases & candidate search, thresholding, and calibration are train/CV-only & holdout tuning or silent reselection \\
+    Holdout scoring & \texttt{evaluation\_summary.json}, \texttt{main\_kpi\_gain\_table.csv} & selected-threshold counts, swept recall, and LCB95 are separate fields & conflating F1 threshold counts with low-FPR recall \\
+    \bottomrule
+  \end{tabular}
+\end{table*}
